<com.inphonik.RX1200 name="Soundtracker" author="William Lamy / Inphonik" comment="In the 90s, hardware samplers were not the only devices capable of composing music with samples. Amiga, Atari, Mac, and PC users were happy to have little programs called soundtrackers that allowed loading audio samples and placing notes on an interface that looks like a spreadsheet. The composers saved their music pieces as Module files and distributed them on their website or via Netlabels.">
